I4_1 (SG 80) at P = (1/4, 1/4, 1/4), which is not a time-reversal-invariant
momentum: time reversal glues one of the two conjugate coreps to itself, and
the trace of the twofold says which.
Bands are counted from 0, as pythtb counts them.

1. the spinful atomic limit
   realized group   : #80.30 I4_11', s orbitals at Wyckoff 4a and 8b, 12 bands
   P                : (0.25, 0.25, 0.25) in the primitive cell,
                      and 2P is no reciprocal-lattice vector
   P valence levels : -2.50036, -2.50036, -2.50036, -2.50036
   χ(E, C2(z))      : (4, 0)
   one fourfold level: spin-independent hoppings commute with every spin
   operator, so this degeneracy is SU(2)'s and decides nothing here

2. what the little group at P allows, and the same table read at -P
   the little group at P, χ(E, C2(z)):
      -P3      dim 1   (1, −i)
      -P4P4    dim 2   (2, 2i)
   the same table read at -P, the point it is printed for, χ(E, C2(z)):
      -P3P3    dim 2   (2, −2i)
      -P4      dim 1   (1, i)
   the two tables are entrywise conjugates: BCS's labels attach to -k, an
   operation taking P to -P interchanges conjugate labels, and the trace is the
   observable

3. i41_soc('generic', lam=0.4): one group-averaged spin-orbit bond set
   realized group   : #80.30 I4_11'
   P valence levels : -2.744031, -2.501964, -2.501964, -2.259907
   degeneracies     : 1 + 2 + 1, level gaps 0.242066 and 0.242057

4. the three levels, each labelled from that one diagonalization
   band 0           : E = -2.744031   χ(E, C2(z)) = (1, −i)   -P3
   bands 1 and 2    : E = -2.501964   χ(E, C2(z)) = (2, 2i)   -P4P4
   band 3           : E = -2.259907   χ(E, C2(z)) = (1, −i)   -P3
   doubled corep    : -P4P4, trace 2i on C2(z), two copies of i
   little group     : 2 unitary elements at P, so no two-dimensional irrep
   the antiunitary glues the irrep with χ(C2(z)) = i to itself, so the pair is
   symmetry-enforced; the -P table read at P makes it two copies of -P4, an
   accidental degeneracy

5. the four valence bands as an elementary band representation
   valence content  : -GM5GM7 + -GM6GM8 + -M5M7 + -M6M8 + 2×-N2N2 + 2×-P3 + -P4P4 + 2×-X3X4
   atomic limit     : 1 x -1E2E↑G(4)@4a(21',2)
   -P4P4 belongs to a labelling of the whole set, not a choice made at P

6. the control: P6_2 at H
   realized group   : #171.122 P6_21', s orbitals at Wyckoff 3a and 6c, 18 bands
   the little group at H, χ(E, C3(z), C3^-1(z)):
      -H4      dim 1   (1, −1, 1)
      -H5H6    dim 2   (2, 1, −1)
   lowest 6 bands   : 2×-H4 + 2×-H5H6 at H
   -H5H6 glues two different irreps; at P -P4P4 glues one to itself

7. the same P-point levels against the spin-orbit strength λ

